# /dev/gunyah is labeled vendor_gunyah_dev by Qualcomm vendor policy (observed on SM6475,
# qualification/gpu/reports/redmi-kunzite-sm6475-host-probe-2026-11-04.txt). AOSP lets crosvm
# open any device carrying the public vm_manager_device_type attribute, and its neverallows keep
# every other coredomain and app away from such devices. Do not relabel the node and do not add
# direct allow rules for other domains.
typeattribute vendor_gunyah_dev vm_manager_device_type;
